{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1551090652,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MTQwMzYwMjA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3178","origin":"github"},"title":"Look out for v7 adjusted branches on subdataset save/add","message":"At the moment we are not considering adjusted branches at all, and treat them like any other branch. I fear that this is not OK. Here is a demo:\n\n```\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/demo % dl rev-create .\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/demo \ncreate(ok): /tmp/demo (dataset)                                                              \n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/demo (git)-[master] % DATALAD_REPO_VERSION=7 dl rev-create sub\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/demo/sub \ncreate(ok): /tmp/demo/sub (dataset)\n(datalad3-dev) 1 mih@meiner /tmp/demo (git)-[master] % git -C sub annex adjust --unlock\nadjust \nSwitched to branch 'adjusted/master(unlocked)'\nok\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/demo (git)-[master] % git -C sub status\nOn branch adjusted/master(unlocked)\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/demo (git)-[master] % dl rev-save\nsave(ok): . (dataset)                                                                        \n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/demo (git)-[master] % git diff HEAD~1 |cat\ndiff --git a/.gitmodules b/.gitmodules\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..c489803\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.gitmodules\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+[submodule \"sub\"]\n+       path = sub\n+       url = ./sub\ndiff --git a/sub b/sub\nnew file mode 160000\nindex 0000000..9ed87e3\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/sub\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+Subproject commit 9ed87e39e73f3b80d17fea655ff880eb7f77fa5f\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/demo (git)-[master] % git -C sub log |cat\ncommit 9ed87e39e73f3b80d17fea655ff880eb7f77fa5f\nAuthor: Michael Hanke \u003cmichael.hanke@gmail.com\u003e\nDate:   Mon Feb 25 11:13:15 2019 +0100\n\n    git-annex adjusted branch\n\ncommit faccd4df8b3b6a6c8e8a25aa4c676cd99e327f55\nAuthor: Michael Hanke \u003cmichael.hanke@gmail.com\u003e\nDate:   Mon Feb 25 11:13:15 2019 +0100\n\n    [DATALAD] new dataset\n```\n\nI believe that the correct thing to do (re a later publish), would be to detect that this is an adjusted branch of `master`, perform a `git annex sync` (or `git annex --unlock`) to bring the actual `master` branch up to speed wrt to the state of the adjusted branch, and then register the state of `master` in the parent.\n\nHowever, this will result in a permanent `modified` status report for the subdataset (despite an empty diff), as it would need to go back to a checkout of the adjusted branch for any actual use.\n\nNot sure at all how to deal with this.\n\nThoughts?","files":null}]}